---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import blinky from "../../../assets/blinky.jpg";
---

<Layout>
    <a href="/projects/" class="backToBtn">Back to Projects</a>

    <div id="tour4" class="tour hidden">
        <h1>Blinky Board!</h1><br /><br />
        <p>
            This is a good example of a specific project page. While it's not
            complicated at all, I think it serves it's purpose. It has an image
            of the project, a short description and the related links like the
            github or tutorial. <br /> Personally I think the Resolution Hardware
            page is a good read, you should go check it out after the tour!<br
            /><br />
        </p>
        <button class="tourBtn" onclick="window.location.replace()">
            rwfsd</button
        >
    </div>

    <div class="projectPage">
        <h1>Blinky Board</h1>
        <img
            src={blinky.src}
            alt="Relatively good blinky board"
            class="largeProjectImg"
        />
        <p>
            While this blinky board looks like... well... shit I choose to keep
            it and show it off for a number of reasons. The main reason being it
            was one of my first projects that I chose to do.
            <br /><br />
            It was made for Hack Club's Blueprint a hardware-based YSWS with a bunch
            of guides for beginners. While my current device couldn't handle Kicad
            it could definetely handle easyEDA so when they released the easyEDA version
            of the blinky guide, I did it almost instantly. The guide was full of
            mistakes but with a bit of asking on slack and googling I was able to
            complete the tutorial and get the project approved.<br /><br />
            After a lot of problems soldering and a lot of dm's sent to Jay, I finished
            the project.<br />
            <br /> I was already addicted to hardware, and I had only just started.
        </p>
        <br />
        <h4>Programs and Links:</h4><br /><br />
        <a
            href="https://blueprint.hackclub.com/projects/1167"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Blueprint!</a
        >
        <a
            href="https://github.com/PL00T00/555-Blinker-board"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Github!</a
        >
    </div>
    <br /><br /><br />
</Layout>
<script>
    const params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);

    if (params.get("tour") === "4") {
        document.getElementById("tour4")?.classList.remove("hidden");
    }
</script>
